In article <IS1CB4EV@math.fu-berlin.de> ezzie@lucs2.lancs.ac.uk (Andrew "Ezzie" Stoker) writes:
>Early in the game, I picked up a wand that I thought was make invisible, so I
>zapped myself, and sure enough it was.  Now, several levels later (dungeon and
>character), I'm still *(&%!)*&%# invisible from one zap, and I don't want it,
>I can't get into shops to buy and sell equipment.  So, how can I get visible
>again?

	You can't.  Your own fault for zapping yourself with the wand.  Next
time zap a monster or your pet (if you have see inv).
	Although, perhaps a suggestion for the game would be to add an
"invisible" flag for each object in the game.  So, maybe Joe Schmoe on level
one will pass right by an "invisible luckstone" without knowing it (or
walking over it).  Plus it would be more realistic.  Anything you have on
your person when you zap yourself should also become invisible, but objects
you find later on would still be visible.
	Plus, then if you wore a visible object, like armor, then the
shopkeeper would let you in since he would know your location.

